$ whaleshark help init    # as the lead agent
whaleshark init [--agent KIND,...] [--keys] [--at-login] [--print-block] [--remove [--all]] [--allow-synced] [--adopt]
  set this project up, check what it needs, and offer the rules for the lead agent

For:      the lead agent, the person, a tab not bound to a run
Flags:    --agent KIND,...  write the rules and the hooks for these agent tools
          --keys            show the shortcuts and, on your yes, write them into your terminals' settings
          --at-login        on Windows, start the engine when you log on
          --print-block     print the rules for the lead agent, and change nothing
          --remove          take out what init wrote for this project
          --all             with --remove, for every project of this login
          --allow-synced    set up a project in a folder synced to other machines
          --adopt           take on a record this login did not make, with its runs and checks  (the person only)
Always:   --json            print the result as JSON
          --run ID          this run, not the open one
          --root DIR        the project in this folder, not the one here
          --help            this help
          --file PATH       the text from this file, or from standard input for -
Exits:    0 done, 3 environment unusable
Example:  whaleshark init --agent claude

Not built yet: it comes with phase 1.
